      year={1986},
      note={Read 2026-07-16 (background survey, not deep-read). Three load-bearing borrowings:
            (1) BREAKDOWN (via Heidegger): tools are transparent in use and become explicit
            objects only when they stop serving; good design reveals breakdowns early and
            productively. Cited in §7 — a refused push is an engineered breakdown: the delta
            served at the cheapest useful moment. A silent merge is a concealed breakdown.
            (2) THE BACKGROUND: meaning arises against unformalizable shared practice; no
            schema captures context. This is the ground for the paper's own no-guarantee
            claim (coherence judged, never computed) — cited as ally at the claim boundary,
            not answered as attack. Reviewers deploying W&F against Sigma hit only systems
            that claim to compute coherence; the paper renounces exactly that. Placed
            2026-08-13 in §3.7 (at "never detects semantic conflict"), §5.5 (validity is no
            fixed predicate) and §5.7 — the last restoring a sentence that carried this
            citation in position.md and was dropped in the carry-over to the whitepaper.
            (3) CONVERSATIONS-FOR-ACTION: their speech-act workflow system (The Coordinator)
            is the ancestor of commitment-typed channels (§6 future work) — cited there
            2026-08-13 as the route from Searle into system design. Note the deeper debt the
            paper does not yet state: Sigma already follows the Coordinator's discipline —
            formalize the structure of commitment, renounce the semantics — so this is
            governing precedent for §3.7 as built, not only a future extension.},
}

